			"type": "text",
			"text": "Amazichthys was an arthrodiran placoderm which lived in the Late Devonian of North Africa, discovered in the Anti-Atlas Mountains of Morrocco in 2022. Its name “Amazigh fish” comes from the Amazigh peoples of North Africa. The species’s holotype is a full body specimen about 90 centimeters long, providing insights on the body forms of larger arthrodiran placoderms such as Dunkelosteus. It was built for high speed, bearing a lunate caudal fin for fast propulsion."
